cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the SAE paper below."
title: "CPYR — Deep Anomaly Detection for In-Vehicle Networks"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation accompanying the SAE WCX 2021 paper "Putting Safety
  of Intended Functionality SOTIF into Practice." A semi-supervised deep
  learning framework for cyber-physical anomaly detection on automotive
  in-vehicle networks, addressing both fuzz-attack detection on Ethernet and
  SOTIF-relevant contextual anomalies on Lane Keep Assist (LKA).
